   129	
   130	Contact orders merely subdivide one path and do not change (2.1).  Nodes and
   131	other multibranch self-singularities create cycles; unibranch cusps attach
   132	trees and can remain invisible.  For two rational sections, the `#S` contact
   133	fibres give `#S` paths and (1.3) gives `bar-P_1=#S-1`, recovering the reviewed
   134	two-section result at its first plurigenus.
   135	
   136	## 3. Sharp countercontrols and the discrepancy gate
   137	
   138	Positive multisection degree alone is insufficient.  Take
   139	
   140	```text
   141	P=P^1_z times P^1_w,
   142	D_infinity={w=infinity},
   143	C=closure({z=w^k}),       k>=2.
   144	```
