   146	Relative to projection to `P^1_z`, `C` is a smooth rational `k`-multisection
   147	meeting the infinity section in one branch, and the boundary graph is a tree.
   148	In fact the complement is exactly `A^2`.  An explicit map is
   149	
   150	```text
   151	(w,t) |-> (w, z=[t:t*w^k+1]),
   152	t=Z0/(Z1-w^k*Z0).
   153	```
   154	
   155	Thus the rational-forest gate is sharp at this type.
   156	
   157	For any embedded log resolution `rho:Xtilde->X`, let
   158	
   159	```text
   160	N_E=v_E(D),
   161	a_E=v_E(K_Xtilde-rho^*K_X),
   162	lambda_E=N_E-a_E-1.
   163	```
   164	
   165	Then, exactly,
   166	
   167	```text
   168	K_Xtilde+Dtilde = rho^*(K_X+D)-sum_E lambda_E E,
   169	
   170	bar-P_n(U)=dim {s in H^0(X,n(K_X+D)):
   171	                v_E(s)>=n*lambda_E for every E}.     (3.1)
   172	```
   173	
   174	For two smooth branches tangent to order `mu`, the successive losses are
   175	`lambda_(E_i)=i-1`.  A unibranch cusp can consume an effective `K+D` without
   176	creating a graph cycle, so (3.1), rather than raw fibre degree or raw
   177	effectivity, is the exact residual gate after the rational-forest test.
   178	
   179	## 4. Homogeneous Miranda incidence geometry
   180	
   181	Suppose a global trace-zero Miranda basis has polynomial coefficients of
   182	common homogenized target degree `d`.  Homogenize in `[u:v:z]` and let
   183	
   184	```text
   185	X_d={Phi^h=0} subset P^2_[u:v:z] times P^1_[X:Y].
   186	```
   187	
   188	Write `A` and `B` for the two hyperplane classes.  The incidence hypersurface
   189	has class `dA+3B`; if it is smooth and irreducible, adjunction gives
   190	
   191	```text
   192	K_(X_d)=(d-3)A+B.                                    (4.1)
   193	```
   194	
   195	For `d>=3`, restriction of ambient sections gives
   196	
   197	```text
   198	p_g(X_d)=h^0(X_d,K_Xd)=(d-1)(d-2)>0.                 (4.2)
   199	```
   200	
   201	Hence no dense open of such a smooth closure admits a dominant `A^2` first
   202	leg.  A surviving presentation of degree at least three must have a singular
   203	or degenerate infinity closure, a reducible/extraneous projective component,
   204	or an actual degree drop after cancellation.  Polynomial changes of Miranda
   205	basis can change presentation degree, so (4.2) is presentationwise, not yet
   206	an intrinsic invariant of the cubic algebra.
   207	
   208	## 5. The first nonlinear family: `d=2`
   209	
   210	A smooth `X_2->P^1` is a conic bundle.  Tsen's theorem gives a rational point
   211	on its generic conic over `C(P^1)`, so `X_2` is rational.  Its infinity curve
   212	
   213	```text
   214	H_infinity=X_2 intersect ({z=0} times P^1)
   215	```
   216	
   217	has bidegree `(2,3)` on `P^1 times P^1`, and is generically smooth of genus
   218	
   219	```text
   220	(2-1)(3-1)=2.
   221	```
   222	
   223	The rational-forest gate therefore excludes the generic quadratic-
   224	coefficient Miranda block from the infinity component alone.
   225	
   226	On the additional projectively finite smooth locus, for
   227	`pi:X_2->P^2`, Hurwitz gives
   228	
   229	```text
   230	R_pi=2A+B,          H_infinity=A,
   231	K_X2+H_infinity+R_pi=2A+2B.                          (5.1)
   232	```
   233	
   234	If `R_pi` is reduced, shares no component with `H_infinity`, and the pair is
   235	generic SNC, adjunction/intersection give
   236	
   237	```text
   238	p_a(H_infinity)=2,
   239	p_a(R_pi)=9,
   240	H_infinity.R_pi=8,
   241	bar-P_1=2+9+(8-1)=18.                                (5.2)
   242	```
   243	
   244	If the reduced pair is log canonical, (5.1) is ample and the complement is
   245	log general type.  If it is not log canonical, (3.1) is the correct test.
   246	Affine fixed-sheet information does not automatically control reducedness,
   247	common components, or singularities at infinity.
   248	
   249	## 6. Exact successor and nonclaims
   250	
   251	The cheapest nonlinear successor is finite:
   252	
   253	1. classify reduced bidegree-`(2,3)` infinity curves whose embedded
   254	   resolution is a rational forest;
   255	2. quarantine nonreduced infinity separately;
   256	3. on each surviving stratum, add the ramification curve and retest the full
   257	   resolved boundary forest; and
   258	4. only then compute higher log plurigenera by the valuation conditions
   259	   (3.1).
   260	
   261	This producer does not exclude every quadratic or higher-degree presentation,
   262	does not make presentation degree intrinsic, and proves no general cubic
   263	block theorem, primitivity statement, map, counterexample, or JC2 result.
   264	Promotion requires a different-model hostile review of (1.1)--(1.3), the
   265	unirational implication, both countercontrols, the adjunction and genus
   266	computations, and every projective-closure hypothesis.
